00:39:04.990 --> 00:39:12.410
Well, Phil Shea found a cooling vest that Steve could wear under his suit to help keep him cool.
幸好，菲尔·谢伊找到了一件冷却背心，让史蒂夫穿在西装里面来保持凉爽。

961
00:39:12.410 --> 00:39:15.770
It's the type of vest that marathon runners and athletes have.
就是马拉松运动员和运动员们穿的那种背心。

962
00:39:15.990 --> 00:39:17.970
They use it to cool their body temperature down.
他们用它来降低体温。

963
00:39:18.150 --> 00:39:20.490
It has these little frozen gel packs.
里面有那种小小的冰冻凝胶包。

964
00:39:20.490 --> 00:39:22.730
And Steve had that on under his suit.
史蒂夫就把那个穿在西装里面。

965
00:39:22.990 --> 00:39:28.150
I've never heard of this thing, which makes sense to me because I would never seek it out.
我以前从没听说过这东西，这也合情合理，因为我绝对不会去找这种东西。

966
00:39:28.430 --> 00:39:31.910
I would never think, how can I be colder in any situation?
我绝不会想，在任何情况下我怎么才能更冷一点？

967
00:39:32.050 --> 00:39:32.510
No, never.
不，绝对不会。

968
00:39:32.670 --> 00:39:33.350
It's a whole thing.
这可是一门大学问。

969
00:39:33.490 --> 00:39:34.050
I Googled it.
我用谷歌搜过了。

970
00:39:34.170 --> 00:39:36.950
There's many different types of cooling vests that you can get.
市面上有许多不同种类的冷却背心。

971
00:39:37.230 --> 00:39:38.190
Athletes use them.
运动员会用它们。

972
00:39:38.930 --> 00:39:40.110
Soldiers use them.
士兵也会用它们。

973
00:39:40.610 --> 00:39:42.610
I mean, you know, it's like a whole thing.
我是说，你知道的，这就像是一门学问。

974
00:39:42.810 --> 00:39:43.870
You know what I do own?
你知道我有什么吗？

975
00:39:44.070 --> 00:39:44.370
What?
什么？

976
00:39:44.670 --> 00:39:45.750
A warming veSt.
发热背心。

977
00:39:46.110 --> 00:39:48.790
I have a vest and you put little hot packs in it.
我有一件背心，你可以把小暖贴放进去。

978
00:39:48.930 --> 00:39:50.170
And it keeps you warm.
它能让你保持温暖。

979
00:39:50.650 --> 00:39:54.090
I bought it so that I could watch my son play ice hockey outdoors.
我买它是为了看我儿子在户外的冰球比赛。

980
00:39:54.530 --> 00:39:54.870
Yeah.
对。

981
00:39:55.130 --> 00:39:58.510
Well, we used to stuff those little hot pocket thingies.
好吧，我们以前会在里面塞那些暖宝宝小玩意儿。

982
00:39:58.590 --> 00:39:59.090
What do you call them?
你们管那叫什么？

983
00:39:59.530 --> 00:40:01.110
Not the food hot pockets.
不是那种食物热口袋（Hot Pockets）。

984
00:40:01.610 --> 00:40:02.650
What are they called?
那叫什么来着？

985
00:40:02.670 --> 00:40:06.450
I love the idea of us having a vest filled with hot pockets, though.
不过我挺喜欢我们穿着塞满热口袋的背心这个主意的。

986
00:40:06.650 --> 00:40:10.030
Because then if you get hungry, it's a snack as well.
因为那样如果你饿了，它也是一份小吃。

987
00:40:10.110 --> 00:40:11.630
It keeps you warm and full.
既能让你保暖又能让你吃饱。

988
00:40:12.030 --> 00:40:16.410
Listen, on the office, I had one skirt that had two little stitch pockets in the back.
听着，在《办公室》片场，我有一条裙子，后面有两个小缝口袋。

989
00:40:16.510 --> 00:40:19.230
And I had one little tiny stitch pocket in the front.
前面还有一个很小很小的缝口袋。

990
00:40:19.390 --> 00:40:21.690
They would give us those little hot pack things.
他们会给我们那些小暖贴。

991
00:40:22.110 --> 00:40:22.890
Little hand warmers?
小暖手宝？

992
00:40:23.090 --> 00:40:23.770
Little hand warmers.
小暖手宝。

993
00:40:24.030 --> 00:40:25.890
I would stick two in my shoes.
我会塞两个在鞋里。

994
00:40:25.910 --> 00:40:28.650
I would stick one in that front pocket, two in my back pocket.
我会塞一个在前口袋里，两个在后口袋里。

995
00:40:28.810 --> 00:40:30.390
I'd stick a few in my bra.
我还会塞几个进文胸里。

996
00:40:30.790 --> 00:40:31.130
Same.
我也是。

997
00:40:31.250 --> 00:40:31.850
Yeah, I remember that.
对，我记得那个。

998
00:40:31.910 --> 00:40:32.090
Yeah.
对。

999
00:40:32.250 --> 00:40:34.650
And if my sweater had pockets, I'd stick them in there.
如果我的毛衣有口袋，我也会塞在里面。

1000
00:40:34.890 --> 00:40:38.610
I'd stick so many of those on my body when we were filming outside when it was cold.
天气冷的时候我们在室外拍戏，我会在身上贴好多那种东西。

1001
00:40:38.610 --> 00:40:41.130
One time, our camera operator, Matt Stone, was like,
有一次，我们的摄像师马特·斯通对我说：

1002
00:40:41.470 --> 00:40:43.030
Ange, just don't take this the wrong way.
安吉，你别介意啊。

1003
00:40:43.030 --> 00:40:45.670
But I can see lumps in your butt on camera.
但我发现在镜头里能看到你屁股上有块状物。

1004
00:40:46.490 --> 00:40:49.550
Like, they don't look human, like human lumps.
就感觉，它们看起来不像是人类那种正常的块状物。

1005
00:40:49.830 --> 00:40:50.750
I was like, dang it.
我当时就想，真是见鬼了。

1006
00:40:50.890 --> 00:40:53.830
And I had to take my little heater things out of my pockets.
然后我不得不把口袋里的小暖贴拿出来。

1007
00:40:54.230 --> 00:40:56.870
Well, I can't believe that they got a cooling veSt.
不过，真不敢相信他们竟然推出了冷却背心。

1008
00:40:56.930 --> 00:40:57.790
And I'm glad they did.
我很高兴他们推出了这个。

1009
00:40:57.950 --> 00:40:58.490
I am too.
我也是。

1010
00:40:58.490 --> 00:40:59.810
I thought that was so smart.
我觉得这太聪明了。

1011
00:40:59.810 --> 00:41:00.370
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1012
00:41:00.810 --> 00:41:02.770
Well, it's time for another weigh-in.
好了，又到了称体重的时候了。

1013
00:41:03.130 --> 00:41:03.910
Big announcement.
重大宣布。

1014
00:41:03.910 --> 00:41:05.630
They lost 31 pounds.
他们减掉了31磅。

1015
00:41:05.990 --> 00:41:06.330
Wow.
哇。

1016
00:41:06.850 --> 00:41:09.490
Michael and Holly are so excited they're going to do a wrap.
迈克尔和霍莉兴奋得要裹保鲜膜了。

1017
00:41:09.710 --> 00:41:13.290
It's the most adorable thing because they're so dorky and cute together.
这太可爱了，因为他们两个在一起既傻气又可爱。

1018
00:41:13.750 --> 00:41:17.750
Well, a little wrap trivia is that they have about 10 minutes of them wrapping.
关于裹保鲜膜的一个小趣闻是，他们拍裹保鲜膜的镜头拍了大约10分钟。

1019
00:41:17.990 --> 00:41:22.350
Even though the part that you see in the show was completely scripted,
尽管你在节目中看到的那个片段完全是按剧本演的，

1020
00:41:22.790 --> 00:41:25.990
even down to Holly, like, rubbing her jacket.
甚至连霍莉揉搓夹克这种细节也是。

1021
00:41:25.990 --> 00:41:28.430
Yeah, yeah, the wiki-wiki-what, all of that was scripted.
对，对，还有什么“威基威基什么”的，那些全都是按剧本演的。

1022
00:41:28.490 --> 00:41:30.990
All of that was scripted, but they did go on and on.
所有这些都是按剧本演的，但他们确实演个没完。

1023
00:41:31.130 --> 00:41:35.550
And Amy Ryan gave an interview where she said this was her favorite scene to shoot
艾米·赖安在一次采访中说，这是她最喜欢拍摄的一场戏，

1024
00:41:35.550 --> 00:41:37.050
because they had so much fun.
因为他们拍得太开心了。

1025
00:41:37.250 --> 00:41:38.770
The crew said the same thing.
剧组人员也这么说。

1026
00:41:38.950 --> 00:41:42.070
They said it was so much fun that those two just went off
他们说太有趣了，那两个人直接即兴发挥了，

1027
00:41:42.070 --> 00:41:44.690
and that the chemistry was just so apparent.
而且那种化学反应是显而易见的。

1028
00:41:44.910 --> 00:41:48.490
I think this was the scene when they were shooting when they realized,
我想这就是他们在拍摄时意识到，

1029
00:41:48.830 --> 00:41:52.130
oh, yeah, these two, true love.
哦，对了，这两个人是真爱的那场戏。

1030
00:41:52.350 --> 00:41:52.570
Yeah.
是啊。

1031
00:41:53.010 --> 00:41:57.330
Well, now it's week three, and there is a new receptionist in town.
好了，现在是第三周，镇上来了一位新接待员。

1032
00:41:57.750 --> 00:41:58.890
Yes, Ronnie.
是的，罗妮。

1033
00:41:59.390 --> 00:42:01.810
Yeah, Ronnie, played by Dale Raul.
对，罗妮，由黛尔·劳尔饰演。

1034
00:42:02.190 --> 00:42:03.730
She has been in a ton of stuff.
她参演过大量的作品。

1035
00:42:03.870 --> 00:42:05.450
She was Maxine in True Blood.
她曾在《真爱如血》中饰演玛克辛。

1036
00:42:05.670 --> 00:42:07.070
Oh, Maxine Fortenberry.
哦，玛克辛·福腾贝里。

1037
00:42:07.270 --> 00:42:08.230
I love True Blood.
我超爱《真爱如血》。

1038
00:42:08.430 --> 00:42:09.410
She was fantastic.
她演得太棒了。

1039
00:42:09.730 --> 00:42:11.010
Of course, you would know that.
你当然会知道了。

1040
00:42:11.130 --> 00:42:11.410
Yes.
是的。

1041
00:42:11.610 --> 00:42:13.570
I have a crossover connection with Dale.
我和黛尔之间还有一次合作交集。

1042
00:42:13.830 --> 00:42:14.290
Tell me.
快告诉我。

1043
00:42:14.450 --> 00:42:16.590
We were both on Fresh Off the Boat.
我们都出演过《初来乍到》。

1044
00:42:16.990 --> 00:42:17.710
Well, there you go.
好吧，原来是这样。

1045
00:42:17.850 --> 00:42:21.210
Not Monk, surprisingly, but Fresh Off the Boat.
出人意料的是不是《神探阿蒙》，而是《初来乍到》。

1046
00:42:21.210 --> 00:42:23.150
Well, she will come back in season six.
嗯，她会在第六季回归。

1047
00:42:23.430 --> 00:42:25.790
This is not the last we're going to see of Ronnie.
我们不会只在这里看到罗妮。

1048
00:42:26.430 --> 00:42:29.910
Meanwhile, we're going to see Pam in her first class.
与此同时，我们要看潘去上第一节课。

1049
00:42:30.170 --> 00:42:31.370
She looks so cute.
她看起来太可爱了。

1050
00:42:31.670 --> 00:42:34.010
She has, like, I'm calling it the college ponytail.
她扎着我称之为“大学马尾辫”的发型。

1051
00:42:34.290 --> 00:42:36.770
She wears this really cute ponytail at school.
她在学校里扎着一个非常可爱的马尾辫。

1052
00:42:37.110 --> 00:42:37.470
All right.
好吧。

1053
00:42:37.570 --> 00:42:40.390
The ponytail is the only thing that's cute about Pam.
那个马尾辫是帕姆身上唯一可爱的地方了。

1054
00:42:40.650 --> 00:42:41.310
Are you kidding?
你在开玩笑吗？

1055
00:42:41.330 --> 00:42:44.010
I thought you looked so cute in all of your college scenes.
我觉得你看上去在所有大学场景里都好可爱。

1056
00:42:44.290 --> 00:42:47.570
Did you notice how young everyone else is in the class?
你注意到班上的其他人有多年轻了吗？

1057
00:42:47.590 --> 00:42:48.750
Oh, you stop it.
噢，别这样。

1058
00:42:48.750 --> 00:42:50.570
No, but this was a deliberate choice.
不是的，但这是一个刻意的选择。

1059
00:42:50.850 --> 00:42:51.410
Well, okay.
好吧，行吧。

1060
00:42:51.830 --> 00:42:53.470
Pam is in her late 20s.
帕姆快三十岁了。

1061
00:42:53.470 --> 00:42:56.110
Do you like how immediately I, like, stand up for my best friend?
你喜欢我这种立刻，怎么说呢，为我最好朋友打抱不平的样子吗？

1062
00:42:56.110 --> 00:42:57.210
I'm like, you stop it.
我就像是，你别这样。

1063
00:42:57.270 --> 00:42:58.170
You are beautiful.
你很漂亮。

1064
00:42:58.530 --> 00:43:00.850
You look just as young as those other ones.
你看上去和那些人一样年轻。

1065
00:43:01.150 --> 00:43:01.200
That's right.
说得对。

1066
00:43:01.270 --> 00:43:02.450
And you are smart.
而且你很聪明。

1067
00:43:03.030 --> 00:43:03.310
Okay.
好的。

1068
00:43:03.310 --> 00:43:03.790
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1069
00:43:03.930 --> 00:43:04.310
You're welcome.
不客气。

1070
00:43:04.590 --> 00:43:07.270
I want you to know I was not being down on myself.
我想让你知道我刚才并不是在贬低自己。

1071
00:43:07.270 --> 00:43:10.690
I was just pointing out a deliberate production choice.
我只是在指出一个刻意的制作选择。

1072
00:43:11.290 --> 00:43:15.610
Pam is in her late 20s, and they made sure that everyone in this class,
帕姆快三十岁了，他们确保这个班上的每一个人，

1073
00:43:15.770 --> 00:43:17.990
that the background performers were all much younger.
也就是背景演员们，都年轻得多。

1074
00:43:17.990 --> 00:43:20.050
They're just starting off in college, right?
他们才刚开始上大学，对吧？

1075
00:43:20.250 --> 00:43:21.530
Pam's going back to school.
帕姆是重返校园。

1076
00:43:21.650 --> 00:43:26.870
And they did want to create this story for Pam that she is kind of, you know.
他们确实想为帕姆创作这样一个故事，就是她有点，你知道的。

1077
00:43:27.870 --> 00:43:28.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1078
00:43:28.590 --> 00:43:29.050
I don't know.
我不知道。

1079
00:43:29.050 --> 00:43:29.670
What am I saying?
我在说什么呢？

1080
00:43:29.690 --> 00:43:30.270
What do they call it?
他们管这叫什么？

1081
00:43:30.310 --> 00:43:31.450
A non-traditional student.
非传统学生。

1082
00:43:31.690 --> 00:43:32.250
There you go.
这就对了。

1083
00:43:32.670 --> 00:43:35.250
Well, not only that, she's in the wrong class.
不仅如此，她还进错班了。

1084
00:43:35.810 --> 00:43:40.590
The teacher, who was played by Sandra Lowe, Professor Monaghan.
那个由桑德拉·洛饰演的老师，莫纳汉教授。

1085
00:43:40.590 --> 00:43:47.670
She's got that zinger of a joke about Zaf Chancery, you know, which, by the way, I read
她讲了一个关于扎夫·钱瑟里的绝妙笑话，你知道的，顺便说一句，我读过

1086
00:43:47.670 --> 00:43:50.430
a Reddit thread where people were like, that doesn't apply.
一个红迪网的帖子，里面的人都在说，那根本不合情理。

1087
00:43:50.850 --> 00:43:51.770
It's wrong.
那是错的。

1088
00:43:52.190 --> 00:43:52.550
Oh.
噢。

1089
00:43:53.190 --> 00:43:53.950
Oh, my.
噢，天哪。

1090
00:43:54.130 --> 00:43:56.350
Well, Pam does not end up leaving the class.
好吧，帕姆最后并没有离开这个班。

1091
00:43:56.470 --> 00:43:57.270
And we got some mail.
而且我们收到了一些邮件。

1092
00:43:57.410 --> 00:44:00.470
People were like, Pam has been so good about standing up for herself.
大家都在说，帕姆在为自己挺身而出这方面一直表现得很棒。

1093
00:44:00.890 --> 00:44:02.570
Why doesn't she just leave the class?
她为什么不直接离开这个班呢？

1094
00:44:02.770 --> 00:44:03.430
I don't know.
我不知道。

1095
00:44:03.430 --> 00:44:04.550
I sympathized.
我很理解。

1096
00:44:04.670 --> 00:44:06.010
I felt like she's new here.
我觉得她是新来的。

1097
00:44:06.010 --> 00:44:07.070
She feels out of place.
她觉得格格不入。

1098
00:44:07.250 --> 00:44:08.710
She just got singled out.
她刚刚被点名了。

1099
00:44:08.850 --> 00:44:12.750
She's going to tuck her head down and know she'll do it right the next time.
她会把头埋起来，心想下次她会做对的。

1100
00:44:12.990 --> 00:44:13.230
Yeah.
是啊。

1101
00:44:13.450 --> 00:44:17.770
But I guess it's going to mean she misses her actual first real class.
不过我猜这意味着她错过了她真正的第一堂正式课。

1102
00:44:19.450 --> 00:44:23.430
Back in the office, Holly hears this coughing, right?
回到办公室里，霍莉听到这阵咳嗽声，对吧？

1103
00:44:23.610 --> 00:44:24.890
She's at her cubicle.
她在自己的工位上。

1104
00:44:25.350 --> 00:44:26.270
Kelly is coughing.
凯莉在咳嗽。

1105
00:44:26.550 --> 00:44:27.630
She sounds sick.
听起来她病了。

1106
00:44:28.110 --> 00:44:31.230
Did you notice on Holly's desk what her nameplate says?
你们有注意到霍莉桌上的名牌写的是什么吗？

1107
00:44:31.510 --> 00:44:32.030
Yes.
注意到了。

1108
00:44:32.850 --> 00:44:33.370
Hollis.
霍利斯。

1109
00:44:33.870 --> 00:44:36.410
And then in quotes, Holly P.
然后带引号写着，霍莉·P。

1110
00:44:37.150 --> 00:44:37.590
Flax.
弗莱克斯。

1111
00:44:38.230 --> 00:44:39.350
I did notice that.
我确实注意到了。

1112
00:44:39.350 --> 00:44:40.330
So that's her real name.
所以那是她的真名。

1113
00:44:40.490 --> 00:44:41.250
Her name is Hollis.
她的名字叫霍利斯。

1114
00:44:41.530 --> 00:44:41.970
Hollis.
霍利斯。

1115
00:44:42.490 --> 00:44:47.690
Kelly has a talking head where she says she's on the third day of her cleanse diet where she's
凯莉有一个面对镜头的独白，说她正在进行排毒减肥法的第三天

1116
00:44:47.690 --> 00:44:51.070
doing the lemon juice, maple syrup, and cayenne pepper and water.
就是喝柠檬汁、枫糖浆、辣椒粉和水。

1117
00:44:51.350 --> 00:44:53.090
That's all she's allowed to have.
那是她唯一能摄入的东西。

1118
00:44:53.710 --> 00:44:55.670
Angela, have you ever done any of these fad diets?
安吉拉，你尝试过这种流行减肥法吗？

1119
00:44:56.050 --> 00:45:00.170
I haven't, but I had a roommate who did something with cayenne pepper and water.
