00:57:47.110 --> 00:57:47.430
Ah!
啊！

1441
00:57:49.220 --> 00:57:49.880
This person!
这个人！

1442
00:57:50.000 --> 00:57:50.940
I don't know!
我不知道！

1443
00:57:52.080 --> 00:57:54.400
Oh, Overly Animated Angela.
哦，过于活泼的安吉拉。

1444
00:57:54.740 --> 00:57:55.680
She was trying.
她一直在努力。

1445
00:57:56.160 --> 00:57:58.480
Maybe he should just do some Mad Libs.
或许他应该去玩填词游戏。

1446
00:57:58.540 --> 00:57:59.260
You love those.
你最喜欢那个了。

1447
00:57:59.500 --> 00:58:04.360
I love Mad Libs and keep suggesting cakes that look like cats or cat accessories.
我喜欢填词游戏，还一直建议做成猫咪或猫咪用品形状的蛋糕。

1448
00:58:04.760 --> 00:58:05.780
It's the way to your heart.
这就是打开你心扉的方式。

1449
00:58:06.140 --> 00:58:08.480
Well, Jim has arrived at Pam's dorm room.
好了，吉姆已经到了帕姆的宿舍门口。

1450
00:58:08.580 --> 00:58:11.280
Did you notice that Pam is the resident advisor?
你注意到帕姆是宿管员了吗？

1451
00:58:11.520 --> 00:58:11.980
I did.
我看了。

1452
00:58:12.160 --> 00:58:13.040
She's the RA!
她是宿管助理！

1453
00:58:13.540 --> 00:58:14.740
It's so perfect.
太完美了。

1454
00:58:15.320 --> 00:58:18.540
It's perfect, but it's also like Pam.
很完美，但也很像帕姆。

1455
00:58:19.040 --> 00:58:20.200
Take on a job.
接了一份工作。

1456
00:58:20.600 --> 00:58:21.320
Come on!
拜托！

1457
00:58:22.320 --> 00:58:24.900
Well, Jim tells the documentary crew, you know what?
吉姆跟纪录片摄制组说，你猜怎么着？

1458
00:58:24.940 --> 00:58:26.740
Why don't you go check out Pam's art over there?
你为什么不去那边看看帕姆的艺术作品呢？

1459
00:58:26.780 --> 00:58:29.940
And when they turn to look for it, he quickly shuts the door, right?
当他们转过头去看的时候，他迅速把门关上了，对吧？

1460
00:58:30.080 --> 00:58:30.340
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1461
00:58:30.680 --> 00:58:34.740
And at 18 minutes, 31 seconds, you hear the cameraman sigh.
在18分31秒的时候，你能听到摄影师叹气。

1462
00:58:35.100 --> 00:58:37.180
You hear Randall Einhorn sigh.
你能听到兰德尔·艾因霍恩叹气。

1463
00:58:37.340 --> 00:58:38.640
Yes, that's Randall!
对，那是兰德尔！

1464
00:58:38.800 --> 00:58:40.100
And that was improvised.
那是即兴发挥。

1465
00:58:40.400 --> 00:58:43.320
He just did that, and they loved it, and they kept it in.
他当时就那么做了，他们很喜欢，就保留了下来。

1466
00:58:43.320 --> 00:58:43.980
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1467
00:58:44.140 --> 00:58:44.740
So fun.
太有趣了。

1468
00:58:44.980 --> 00:58:51.420
I would like to say, Pam, thank you for finally wearing a hoodie or any kind of casual clothing
我想说，帕姆，谢谢你终于在艺术学校

1469
00:58:51.420 --> 00:58:52.660
here at art school.
这里穿了连帽衫或任何休闲服装。

1470
00:58:52.880 --> 00:58:56.260
I feel like she just has been overdressed since she got there.
我觉得她自打去那儿之后就一直穿得过于正式了。

1471
00:58:56.300 --> 00:58:58.020
We are on two different pages on this.
在这点上我们俩看法完全不同。

1472
00:58:58.140 --> 00:59:00.720
I think that Pam has looked amazing for art school.
我觉得帕姆在艺校的装扮看起来棒极了。

1473
00:59:01.000 --> 00:59:02.480
I love her ponytail.
我喜欢她的马尾辫。

1474
00:59:02.940 --> 00:59:08.140
I just think, and this was a choice that, I should say that, this has all been a choice.
我只是觉得——这是一个选择，我应该说，这一切都是个选择。

1475
00:59:08.140 --> 00:59:09.140
It's on purpose.
这是故意的。

1476
00:59:09.420 --> 00:59:14.760
It's all to make her stand out a little bit, to be like, she isn't dressing the way the
这一切都是为了让她显得有点与众不同，就好像，她穿得跟现在

1477
00:59:14.760 --> 00:59:16.400
young people dress today.
年轻人穿的不一样。

1478
00:59:16.520 --> 00:59:16.800
Right.
对吧。

1479
00:59:17.020 --> 00:59:17.260
Okay?
好吗？

1480
00:59:17.320 --> 00:59:21.060
So, like, I'm giving her grief about it, but you guys, we planned this.
所以，我拿这个取笑她，但是伙计们，这是我们计划好的。

1481
00:59:21.200 --> 00:59:21.400
Right.
对。

1482
00:59:21.480 --> 00:59:24.860
And also her affected speech, how she's like, top of the morning, Tilia.
还有她那做作的说话方式，她会说，早啊，蒂莉娅。

1483
00:59:25.500 --> 00:59:26.480
Shall we walk over here?
我们往那边走走好吗？

1484
00:59:26.620 --> 00:59:27.460
Perhaps we'll sit here.
也许我们坐这儿。

1485
00:59:28.000 --> 00:59:30.040
Let me cross my legs in my stockings.
让我穿着丝袜盘起腿来。

1486
00:59:30.480 --> 00:59:31.460
What are you talking about?
你在说什么呢？

1487
00:59:31.640 --> 00:59:32.500
That's how she talks.
她就是那样说话的。

1488
00:59:32.500 --> 00:59:33.440
No, she does not.
不，她才没有。

1489
00:59:34.360 --> 00:59:35.340
What are you doing?
你在干什么？

1490
00:59:35.520 --> 00:59:36.620
I'm just messing with you.
我只是跟你开玩笑呢。

1491
00:59:36.620 --> 00:59:37.520
I really got worried.
我真的开始担心了。

1492
00:59:37.540 --> 00:59:38.380
I was like, what?
我当时想，什么？

1493
00:59:39.040 --> 00:59:40.420
I am messing with you.
我是在逗你呢。

1494
00:59:40.780 --> 00:59:45.200
I don't know how long Jim and Pam got to hang out and smooch, but Pam got a knock on
我不知道吉姆和帕姆能腻在一起亲热多久，但帕姆的门

1495
00:59:45.200 --> 00:59:45.580
her door.
被人敲响了。

1496
00:59:45.880 --> 00:59:50.040
There was some girl mad at another girl because someone took someone's soy milk.
有个女孩生另一个女孩的气，因为有人拿了别人的豆浆。

1497
00:59:50.220 --> 00:59:55.460
And now Jim is in, like, the dorm room common area at 18 minutes, 55 seconds.
现在吉姆在宿舍的公共区域，时间是18分55秒。

1498
00:59:56.080 --> 00:59:58.240
Yeah, he's watching a baseball game.
对，他在看棒球比赛。

1499
00:59:58.240 --> 01:00:04.820
Yes, and Jenna, you can very faintly hear some sort of baseball commentators, like announcers,
是的，珍娜，你能隐约听到某种棒球解说员的声音，就像播音员，

1500
01:00:05.020 --> 01:00:05.700
sports announcers.
体育解说员。

1501
01:00:05.880 --> 01:00:06.060
Yeah.
没错。

1502
01:00:06.420 --> 01:00:11.040
Those were played by our very own producer, James O'Kerry and Eric Colgen.
那是我们的专属制片人詹姆斯·奥凯里和埃里克·科尔根演奏的。

1503
01:00:11.300 --> 01:00:11.700
All right.
好的。

1504
01:00:11.840 --> 01:00:15.080
See, I wondered, is that a real baseball game?
你看，我在想，那是真正的棒球比赛吗？

1505
01:00:15.220 --> 01:00:19.160
So, it's obviously real baseball footage, but then we put our own commentators on it.
所以，这显然是真实的棒球录像，但我们配上了自己的解说员。

1506
01:00:19.220 --> 01:00:19.940
That's right.
没错。

1507
01:00:20.260 --> 01:00:22.200
So, Jenna and I have been in touch with James.
所以，珍娜和我一直跟詹姆斯保持着联系。

1508
01:00:22.400 --> 01:00:23.080
He is fantastic.
他太棒了。

1509
01:00:23.080 --> 01:00:25.580
He was that guy that could, like, get you anything on set.
他就是那种在片场什么都能给你搞定的人。

1510
01:00:25.580 --> 01:00:27.300
If you needed it, James got it.
如果你需要什么，詹姆斯都能弄到。

1511
01:00:27.300 --> 01:00:31.260
And we had lots of questions for him, and he answered them for this episode.
我们向他提出了很多问题，他都在这一集里解答了。

1512
01:00:31.520 --> 01:00:33.080
He even had the shooting draft.
他甚至还保留着拍摄剧本。

1513
01:00:33.300 --> 01:00:34.560
James, thank you so much.
詹姆斯，非常感谢你。

1514
01:00:34.740 --> 01:00:36.440
I feel like we might have a Jamesopedia.
我觉得我们可能拥有了一个“詹姆斯百科”。

1515
01:00:37.100 --> 01:00:38.820
Yeah, it couldn't come at a better time.
是啊，来得正是时候。

1516
01:00:39.160 --> 01:00:39.600
Yeah.
是啊。

1517
01:00:39.960 --> 01:00:42.920
You know, because we don't have Kentopedia anymore, James.
你知道的，因为我们不再有“肯特百科”了，詹姆斯。

1518
01:00:43.780 --> 01:00:47.500
James Carey, will you be our Jamesopedia?
詹姆斯·凯里，你愿意成为我们的“詹姆斯百科”吗？

1519
01:00:49.670 --> 01:00:52.170
Should we talk about Stanley's birthday?
我们该聊聊斯坦利的生日了吗？

1520
01:00:52.670 --> 01:00:54.310
I mean, it looks a little sad.
我的意思是，看起来有点凄凉。

1521
01:00:54.730 --> 01:00:56.310
Everyone's standing around eating fruit.
大家都站在周围吃水果。

1522
01:00:56.310 --> 01:00:58.330
Ronnie wants to know if anyone wants to dance.
罗妮想知道有没有人想跳舞。

1523
01:00:58.590 --> 01:01:02.750
By the way, my Dolly Parton fans, did you catch the song playing?
顺便问一下，我的多莉·帕顿粉丝们，你们听到播出的歌了吗？

1524
01:01:02.930 --> 01:01:03.370
Oh, yeah.
哦，听到了。

1525
01:01:03.870 --> 01:01:05.350
Here you come again.
你又来了。

1526
01:01:05.690 --> 01:01:06.930
I love that song.
我超喜欢那首歌。

1527
01:01:07.050 --> 01:01:08.010
I love that song, too.
我也很喜欢那首歌。

1528
01:01:08.030 --> 01:01:10.310
I went and listened to it after I watched the episode.
看完这一集后我还特意去听了。

1529
01:01:10.670 --> 01:01:13.290
It's not the song I would play at a birthday party.
这不是我会在生日派对上放的歌。

1530
01:01:13.810 --> 01:01:14.290
No.
不是。

1531
01:01:14.630 --> 01:01:15.050
No.
不是。

1532
01:01:16.270 --> 01:01:17.130
Probably not.
大概不会吧。

1533
01:01:17.890 --> 01:01:19.510
But I love that song.
但我就是喜欢那首歌。

1534
01:01:19.850 --> 01:01:25.410
People are going to sneak off from this party, and they're going to have some cake in the
人们会从这个派对上溜走，然后去吃点蛋糕在

1535
01:01:25.410 --> 01:01:25.850
warehouse.
仓库里。

1536
01:01:26.230 --> 01:01:29.350
The warehouse is the sneak site, clearly.
仓库很显然就是偷情地点。

1537
01:01:30.230 --> 01:01:30.650
Clearly.
显而易见。

1538
01:01:31.010 --> 01:01:36.370
And I mean, isn't Angela uncomfortable being in that room with all those other people,
我的意思是，安吉拉跟那么多其他人待在那个房间里，难道不觉得别扭吗，

1539
01:01:36.530 --> 01:01:37.570
including her fiance?
包括她的未婚夫？

1540
01:01:38.370 --> 01:01:40.190
She doesn't have any guilt about it.
她一点罪恶感也没有。

1541
01:01:40.290 --> 01:01:41.010
I guess not.
我想是没有的。

1542
01:01:41.230 --> 01:01:42.650
She has no problem sleeping at night.
她晚上睡觉可安稳了。

1543
01:01:42.770 --> 01:01:43.590
We've established that.
这一点我们已经证实过了。

1544
01:01:43.590 --> 01:01:44.150
That's true.
确实如此。

1545
01:01:44.950 --> 01:01:48.230
Stanley is in the room with the cake, but he's not even eating it.
斯坦利也在放蛋糕的房间里，但他甚至都没吃。

1546
01:01:48.390 --> 01:01:49.810
He said his tastes have changed.
他说他的口味变了。

1547
01:01:50.210 --> 01:01:54.710
Now all he likes is baklava, which I thought was a really interesting thing to say, because
现在他只喜欢果仁蜜饼，我觉得这句话真的很有意思，因为

1548
01:01:54.710 --> 01:01:56.850
baklava is very, very, very sweet.
果仁蜜饼是非常非常非常甜的。

1549
01:01:57.130 --> 01:01:58.710
Like, if you've lost your sweet tooth.
就好像，如果你已经戒了甜食的话。

1550
01:01:58.850 --> 01:01:59.650
I mean, it's nutty.
我的意思是，里面有很多坚果。

1551
01:02:00.390 --> 01:02:01.610
I love a baklava.
我喜欢果仁蜜饼。

1552
01:02:01.710 --> 01:02:02.130
I do, too.
我也喜欢。

1553
01:02:02.210 --> 01:02:03.050
It's dense, though.
不过它很瓷实。

1554
01:02:03.250 --> 01:02:05.230
It's a dense, sugary treat.
这是一种瓷实又含糖量高的甜点。

1555
01:02:05.670 --> 01:02:06.330
I know.
我知道。

1556
01:02:06.450 --> 01:02:09.450
And I often eat too much of it, and I get a stomach ache.
而且我经常吃太多，然后就会胃疼。

1557
01:02:09.450 --> 01:02:14.910
Because, you know, they give you a tiny piece, and I'll eat like five of them, because they're
因为，你知道的，他们只给你很小的一块，而我会连吃个五块左右，因为它们

1558
01:02:14.910 --> 01:02:15.610
just so good.
实在是太好吃了。

1559
01:02:15.890 --> 01:02:17.290
Well, that's what happens with you.
行吧，你就是这样。

1560
01:02:17.510 --> 01:02:19.130
You're always like, Ange, look how cute.
你总是说，安吉，看这个多可爱。

1561
01:02:19.170 --> 01:02:19.810
It's so tiny.
它太小了。

1562
01:02:20.270 --> 01:02:20.810
I know.
我知道。

1563
01:02:20.890 --> 01:02:22.350
And then you're like, Ange, I have a stomach ache.
然后你就说，安吉，我胃疼。

1564
01:02:22.610 --> 01:02:22.990
I know.
我知道。

1565
01:02:23.590 --> 01:02:27.710
Dwight, Holly, Michael, and Ronnie spy on the group.
德怀特、霍莉、迈克尔和罗妮在暗中监视这群人。

1566
01:02:28.090 --> 01:02:29.950
Dwight's like, they should not be in there.
德怀特说，他们不该待在里面。

1567
01:02:30.090 --> 01:02:30.350
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1568
01:02:30.550 --> 01:02:31.910
You know why he's saying that.
你知道他为什么这么说。

1569
01:02:32.550 --> 01:02:35.190
And Michael says, we should have our own party.
然后迈克尔说，我们该办我们自己的派对。

1570
01:02:35.290 --> 01:02:36.730
Let's all go play mini golf.
我们一起去玩迷你高尔夫吧。

1571
01:02:36.730 --> 01:02:40.490
Both Ronnie and Michael and Dwight and Holly.
罗妮和迈克尔，还有德怀特和霍莉。

1572
01:02:40.710 --> 01:02:41.470
That foursome.
那四个人。

1573
01:02:41.810 --> 01:02:43.110
Oh, I wish that happened.
哦，我真希望这一幕发生了。

1574
01:02:43.210 --> 01:02:43.790
Me, too.
我也是。

1575
01:02:44.330 --> 01:02:46.750
Well, Holly can't go because she has a date tonight.
不过，霍莉去不了，因为她今晚有约会。

1576
01:02:47.490 --> 01:02:47.670
Mm.
嗯。

1577
01:02:47.930 --> 01:02:50.190
And then Michael has the sweetest talking head.
然后迈克尔有一段特别温馨的单人采访。

1578
01:02:50.390 --> 01:02:51.910
He's like, Holly doesn't need any luck.
他说，霍莉根本不需要什么运气。

1579
01:02:52.230 --> 01:02:54.690
Everyone who meets her instantly loves her.
所有见到她的人都会立刻喜欢上她。

1580
01:02:55.570 --> 01:02:55.810
Yeah.
对啊。

1581
01:02:56.070 --> 01:02:56.830
So cute.
太可爱了。

1582
01:02:56.850 --> 01:02:58.690
I want these two kids to get together.
我真希望这两个人能在一起。

1583
01:02:59.250 --> 01:03:03.530
Angela, I have a question for you about the next scene, which is when Dwight busts in
安吉，关于下一场戏，我有个问题想问你，就是德怀特闯进来

1584
01:03:03.530 --> 01:03:04.970
and he kicks over the cake.
并且踢翻了蛋糕的那场戏。

1585
01:03:04.970 --> 01:03:05.390
Yeah.
对。

1586
01:03:05.730 --> 01:03:06.690
I wasn't there.
我当时不在场。

1587
01:03:06.870 --> 01:03:07.590
I'm at art school.
我在艺术学校。

1588
01:03:07.890 --> 01:03:09.230
What was it like to shoot that scene?
拍摄那场戏是什么感觉？

1589
01:03:09.390 --> 01:03:10.030
Here's the thing.
情况是这样的。

1590
01:03:10.370 --> 01:03:15.330
That room was like, I mean, Jenna, it was like six feet by six feet.
那个房间，我是说，珍娜，大概只有六英尺乘六英尺见方。

1591
01:03:15.750 --> 01:03:17.190
It is really small.
真的很小。

1592
01:03:17.190 --> 01:03:18.490
And we were all in there.
我们当时全都在里面。

1593
01:03:18.650 --> 01:03:23.250
They tried to put chairs in so that we could sit, but not everyone could sit, obviously.
他们试图放几把椅子让我们坐，但显然不是所有人都能坐。

1594
01:03:23.410 --> 01:03:23.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1595
01:03:23.970 --> 01:03:25.410
We were pretty crammed in.
我们挤得满满当当的。

1596
01:03:25.550 --> 01:03:27.750
I remember I couldn't look at Phyllis or I would laugh.
我记得我不能看菲利斯，否则我就会笑场。

1597
01:03:28.090 --> 01:03:28.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1598
01:03:28.850 --> 01:03:32.630
Whenever she had her exchange with Michael, she would kind of start to break a little.
每当她和迈克尔有对手戏时，她就会有点快要演不下去了。

1599
01:03:32.630 --> 01:03:37.630
And then Rain kicked over that cake with such, like, force.
然后雷恩带着十足的力道把那个蛋糕给踢翻了。

1600
01:03:37.910 --> 01:03:38.030
Yeah.
对啊。

1601
01:03:38.130 --> 01:03:39.350
It went flying.
它飞了出去。

1602
01:03:39.750 --> 01:03:41.430
We all got cake on us.
我们身上都沾满了蛋糕。

1603
01:03:41.850 --> 01:03:43.370
And then they would have to clean it up.
然后他们就得把它们清理干净。

1604
01:03:43.490 --> 01:03:46.610
We couldn't do it very many times because we were like, Rain, do you have to kick it
我们没法拍太多次，因为我们当时在想，雷恩，你非得把它踢得

1605
01:03:46.610 --> 01:03:47.330
that hard?
那么用力吗？

1606
01:03:48.590 --> 01:03:52.670
So pretty much, I just remember being crammed in and trying not to laugh.
所以差不多，我只记得当时挤在一起，努力忍住不笑。

1607
01:03:52.930 --> 01:03:55.310
Well, I thought that scene looked like it was a lot of fun to shoot.
嗯，我觉得那个场景拍起来肯定很有意思。

1608
01:03:55.310 --> 01:03:59.930
And I know, don't ask Rain Wilson to kick something unless you really want it kicked.
而且我知道，千万别让雷恩·威尔逊去踢什么东西，除非你真的想让它飞出去。

1609
01:04:00.110 --> 01:04:01.730
Yeah, unless you want it to go flying.
对，除非你想让它飞走。

1610
01:04:01.930 --> 01:04:02.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1611
01:04:02.170 --> 01:04:06.810
I don't think they anticipated that that much cake would travel because it was quite a cleanup.
我想他们没想到会有那么多蛋糕飞溅出来，因为清理起来相当费劲。

1612
01:04:07.070 --> 01:04:10.010
Well, now it is week five of the weight loss competition.
好了，现在是减肥比赛的第五周。

1613
01:04:10.290 --> 01:04:12.370
The Scranton branch is not doing very well.
斯克兰顿分公司表现得不是很好。

1614
01:04:13.010 --> 01:04:18.370
Holly tells us that corporate has now upped the prize to five vacation days.
霍莉告诉我们，总公司现在把奖品提高到了五天带薪假。

1615
01:04:18.920 --> 01:04:21.170
But things are breaking down between people.
但人际关系开始出现裂痕了。

1616
01:04:21.350 --> 01:04:22.410
I mean, Kevin's in the kitchen.
我是说，凯文在厨房里。

1617
01:04:22.590 --> 01:04:24.470
He's making himself a peanut butter bagel.
他正在给自己做一个花生酱百吉饼。

1618
01:04:24.750 --> 01:04:27.250
Creed and Kelly are glaring at him.
克里德和凯莉正恶狠狠地盯着他。

1619
01:04:27.470 --> 01:04:33.010
Oh, there's a deleted scene where Meredith and Kelly and Holly are working on the dry erase
哦，有一个被删减的片段，讲的是梅雷迪思、凯利和霍莉在白板上

1620
01:04:33.010 --> 01:04:33.350
board.
工作。

1621
01:04:33.510 --> 01:04:33.730
Yeah.
对。

1622
01:04:34.350 --> 01:04:37.210
And Kelly goes, I'm doing a blood type diet.
然后凯利说，我在实行血型减肥法。

1623
01:04:37.410 --> 01:04:38.830
And Meredith goes, who gives a f***?
然后梅雷迪思说，谁他妈在乎？

1624
01:04:39.270 --> 01:04:41.170
And Kelly goes, what'd you say, whore?
然后凯利说，你刚才说什么，贱货？

1625
01:04:41.310 --> 01:04:42.390
And Holly goes, I got it.
然后霍莉说，我懂了。

1626
01:04:42.450 --> 01:04:42.590
Okay.
好吧。

1627
01:04:42.650 --> 01:04:43.330
Hey, hey, hey.
嘿，嘿，嘿。

1628
01:04:43.690 --> 01:04:44.770
Oh my gosh.
噢天哪。

1629
01:04:44.770 --> 01:04:46.810
I mean, things are getting really intense.
我是说，事情变得越来越白热化了。

1630
01:04:47.170 --> 01:04:51.990
They're so intense that Kelly says in a talking head that she swallowed a tapeworm last night
局势如此紧张，以至于凯利在一个访谈中说她昨晚吞下了一条

1631
01:04:51.990 --> 01:04:53.910
that Creed gave her from Mexico.
克里德从墨西哥带给她的绦虫。

1632
01:04:54.390 --> 01:04:58.290
Kelly, why would you swallow a worm Creed gave you?
凯利，你为什么会吞下克里德给你的虫子？

1633
01:04:58.690 --> 01:04:59.090
I know.
我知道。

1634
01:04:59.230 --> 01:05:00.650
Creed says it wasn't a tapeworm.
克里德说那不是绦虫。

1635
01:05:00.930 --> 01:05:03.810
Angela, I'll have you know, I looked it up.
安吉拉，我得告诉你，我查过了。

1636
01:05:03.970 --> 01:05:04.230
Yeah.
对。

1637
01:05:04.670 --> 01:05:07.710
The tapeworm diet is a real thing.
绦虫减肥法是真实存在的。

1638
01:05:08.070 --> 01:05:09.330
Oh God, really?
天哪，真的吗？

1639
01:05:09.690 --> 01:05:14.530
Well, it's obviously illegal in the United States and it's totally dangerous.
嗯，这在美国显然是非法的，而且极其危险。

1640
01:05:14.770 --> 01:05:16.030
Where are they doing it?
他们在哪儿搞这个？

1641
01:05:16.170 --> 01:05:21.550
I don't know, but I guess you can buy pills that have a tapeworm egg inside of it.
我不知道，但我想你可以买到里面有绦虫卵的药丸。

1642
01:05:21.730 --> 01:05:22.650
Don't do this.
千万别这么做。

1643
01:05:22.830 --> 01:05:23.230
No.
不。

1644
01:05:23.510 --> 01:05:30.150
I read on Healthline that it doesn't even work because yes, it feeds off your body's nutrients,
我在健康热线网站上看到，这根本没用，因为没错，它会消耗你身体的营养，

1645
01:05:30.330 --> 01:05:32.690
but it feeds off the good stuff too, right?
但它也会消耗好的营养，对吧？

1646
01:05:32.710 --> 01:05:34.450
It doesn't just eat your fat, everybody.
大家听着，它不只是吃你的脂肪。

1647
01:05:34.450 --> 01:05:37.350
It eats everything and you get really sick.
它什么都吃，而且你会病得非常重。

1648
01:05:37.490 --> 01:05:42.030
You can get diarrhea, abdominal pain, nausea, fever, weakness.
你可能会腹泻、腹痛、恶心、发烧、虚弱。

1649
01:05:42.030 --> 01:05:44.550
You can also get bacterial infections.
你还可能会感染细菌。

1650
01:05:44.550 --> 01:05:46.830
You can get neurological issues.
你可能会出现神经系统问题。

1651
01:05:47.430 --> 01:05:49.790
Most of these pills are a scam.
大多数这类药丸都是骗人的。

1652
01:05:50.250 --> 01:05:50.730
Okay.
好吧。

1653
01:05:50.810 --> 01:05:57.770
They do not really have a tapeworm, but a woman in Iowa swallowed a real one and she got super
它们其实没有绦虫，但爱荷华州的一个女人吞了一条真的，结果病得

1654
01:05:57.770 --> 01:06:00.930
sick and she had to confess to her doctor what she did.
非常严重，她不得不向医生坦白自己做的事。

1655
01:06:01.090 --> 01:06:03.550
He had to report it to the State Department.
他不得不向国务院报告此事。

1656
01:06:03.790 --> 01:06:05.130
It was a whole crazy thing.
整个事情简直荒唐透顶。

1657
01:06:05.570 --> 01:06:07.210
He didn't even know how to kill it.
他甚至不知道该怎么杀死它。

1658
01:06:07.210 --> 01:06:08.150
It was a whole thing.
总之就是一团糟。

1659
01:06:08.650 --> 01:06:15.430
Guys, do not swallow a tapeworm on purpose are words I'm saying just in case anyone out
各位，“千万不要故意吞下一条绦虫”，我这句话是说给万一有谁

1660
01:06:15.430 --> 01:06:16.790
there thought they should.
觉得应该这么做的人听的。

1661
01:06:17.830 --> 01:06:24.370
You know, Jenna, I have a tapeworm story, but you know I'm going to save it for the finale.
你知道吗，珍娜，我有一个关于绦虫的故事，但我打算把它留到大结局时再讲。

1662
01:06:24.750 --> 01:06:28.830
When we are done with the whole run of the office, you will remember.
等我们把整季《办公室》播完，你就会想起来的。

1663
01:06:29.070 --> 01:06:30.770
I don't want to spoil it.
我不想剧透。

1664
01:06:30.890 --> 01:06:32.750
There is a scene in the finale.
大结局里有一场戏。

1665
01:06:32.910 --> 01:06:34.530
I don't want to spoil it.
我不想剧透。

1666
01:06:34.530 --> 01:06:38.590
But you'll remember, Jenna, Rain and I traded tapeworm stories.
但你会记起来的，珍娜，雷恩和我交换了绦虫的故事。

1667
01:06:38.870 --> 01:06:40.470
I'm saving it for the finale.
我把它留到大结局再讲。

1668
01:06:40.950 --> 01:06:49.370
Guys, if you've ever had a reason to tune in to at least our finale episode of Office
各位，如果你们曾经有过任何理由去收听我们《办公室女士》的压轴大结局，

1669
01:06:49.370 --> 01:06:51.370
Ladies, you have it now.
女士们，你们现在有了。

1670
01:06:51.590 --> 01:06:57.310
There is a real life Angela Rain moment that happens behind the scenes of the finale.
大结局的幕后发生了一个现实生活中的安吉拉与雷恩时刻。

1671
01:06:57.790 --> 01:06:59.410
It involves a tapeworm.
它跟绦虫有关。

1672
01:06:59.730 --> 01:07:01.170
We'll get to it.
我们待会儿会聊到。

1673
01:07:01.450 --> 01:07:04.310
Well, guys, that's weight loss part one.
好了，各位，这就是减重篇（上）。

1674
01:07:05.410 --> 01:07:12.130
We will be back next week with weight loss part two when Jim has a big surprise for Pam.
我们下周将带着减重篇（下）回归，届时吉姆会给帕姆一个巨大的惊喜。

1675
01:07:12.290 --> 01:07:13.670
We're going to tell you all about it.
我们会把一切都告诉你们。

1676
01:07:13.950 --> 01:07:15.850
Aw, jam fans.
哦，吉姆和帕姆的粉丝们。

1677
01:07:16.050 --> 01:07:17.130
You don't want to miss it.
你们可千万别错过。

1678
01:07:17.530 --> 01:07:18.170
See you then.
到时候见。

1679
01:07:18.310 --> 01:07:18.670
See ya.
再见。

1680
01:07:22.390 --> 01:07:24.850
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies Second Drink.
感谢收听《办公室女士》第二杯。

